"Marky Mark" <mdmota@yahoo.com.au> wrote:
>No whilst this was very handy, I think this is unintended behaviour, if
>luck affects your ability to hit something with a weapon or barehanded,
>I think it should also affect your chances to kick something, dont you
>agree?

Kicks work *very* differently to weapon attacks.  In particular, it
appears (and a cursory test in explore mode doesn't immediately
contradict this) that your kick will *always* hit if any of the
following are true:
 * The target monster is trapped.
 * The target monster cannot see.
 * The target monster is an sea monster.
 * The target monster does not have eyes.
 * The target monster is paralysed, stunned, confused, or sleeping.
 * The target monster's speed is less than 12.

Superseded to add: I missed a bit.  That's the monster's chance to evade
the kick.  Your chance to land it in the right place to begin with is
based on the amount you are carrying.  If your total burden is less than
70% of the maximum you can carry without being Burdened or worse, you
always land it in the right place; otherwise, there's some
randomisation.
